{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2665","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2665","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2665\",\"parent_revision\":\"54c84577f05d410992e7a3cfd2ff4ee71ce7aa74c4c5741b715431765c0d27db\",\"root_revision\":\"54c84577f05d410992e7a3cfd2ff4ee71ce7aa74c4c5741b715431765c0d27db\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-07-08\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`_rename_item_title` (operations.py ~line 722) and `_apply_plan_to_item` (operations.py ~line 770) both call `parse_issue_number(issue_ref)` and raise `ValueError` when the result is `None` \u2014 the same pattern that was fixed in `close_item` (#2656 fix, commit 600e3e1e).\\n\\nCurrently these helpers are only called after a `try_get_github()` check returns a real `Repository` object, so beads nanoids cannot reach them \u2014 `try_get_github` returns `None` for the beads backend and callers check for that. The ValueError is therefore not triggered in practice today.\\n\\nHowever, if the call paths to these helpers change (or a future caller does not guard on `try_get_github`), beads nanoids would hit the same crash. The safe pattern \u2014 already used in `resolve_item` and now in `close_item` \u2014 is to skip the GitHub-specific action when `issue_num_val is None` rather than raise.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:24:24.551186Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: _rename_item_title raises ValueError when parse_issue_number returns None for a beads nanoid\\nevidence: Read(backlog_core/operations.py:715-745) \u2014 code at line ~722: `if num is None: msg = f\\\"Invalid issue ref: {issue_ref!r}\\\"; raise ValueError(msg)` \u2014 confirmed in source\\nsource: backlog_core/operations.py lines 715-745\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: ValueError is not caught by the except (GithubException, BacklogError) clause in _rename_item_title\\nevidence: Read(backlog_core/operations.py:715-745) \u2014 except clause explicitly names only GithubException and BacklogError; ValueError is not a subclass of either\\nsource: backlog_core/operations.py lines 715-745\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: _apply_plan_to_item has the same raise ValueError pattern\\nevidence: Read(backlog_core/operations.py:763-810) \u2014 identical structure: parse_issue_number called, None check raises ValueError, caught only by except (GithubException, BacklogError)\\nsource: backlog_core/operations.py lines 763-810\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Current code is protected by try_get_github() returning None for beads backends\\nevidence: Read(backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py:159) \u2014 issue_id_type = \\\"string\\\"; try_get_github() returns None for non-GitHub backends; if repository is not None: guard in both functions prevents entry\\nsource: backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py line 159\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Safe skip pattern (warn + return instead of raise) is already used in _auto_register_plan_artifact\\nevidence: Read(backlog_core/operations.py:787+) \u2014 `if issue_number is None: out.warn(...); return` \u2014 no raise\\nsource: backlog_core/operations.py line ~787\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Same safe pattern was applied to close_item in commit 600e3e1e for issue #2656\\nevidence: item description references commit 600e3e1e and PR #2656 as the prior fix; pattern in close_item confirms it\\nsource: backlog item #2665 description; backlog_core/operations.py close_item function\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:23:37.086802Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: _rename_item_title and _apply_plan_to_item raise ValueError for beads nanoid issue refs\\nDate: 2026-06-21\\nGoal: Determine whether information is complete to plan and implement the fix for the latent ValueError crash path in _rename_item_title and _apply_plan_to_item when issue_ref is a beads nanoid\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Root cause location in operations.py | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(operations.py:715-745) \u2014 _rename_item_title raises ValueError(\\\"Invalid issue ref\\\") at line ~722 when parse_issue_number returns None; same pattern at _apply_plan_to_item lines 763-810\\n2. ValueError is not caught by except clause | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(operations.py:715-745) \u2014 except (GithubException, BacklogError) does NOT include ValueError; the raise propagates uncaught\\n3. Current protection mechanism (try_get_github returns None for beads) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py:159) \u2014 issue_id_type = \\\"string\\\"; try_get_github() returns None for non-GitHub backends, so the if repository is not None: guard prevents entry into the vulnerable code path\\n4. Safe skip pattern already established | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read(operations.py:787+) \u2014 _auto_register_plan_artifact uses: if issue_number is None: out.warn(...); return \u2014 no raise; same pattern in close_item after commit 600e3e1e (#2656 fix)\\n5. Fix scope and files | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: operations.py _rename_item_title (~line 722) and _apply_plan_to_item (~line 770) \u2014 two call sites; replace raise ValueError with out.warn + return\\n6. Test gap | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep(tests/) \u2014 no test exercises _rename_item_title or _apply_plan_to_item with a beads nanoid issue_ref; new tests needed for the skip path\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- All conditions were AVAILABLE at snapshot; no changes\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_rename_item_title` \u2014 raises ValueError for non-numeric issue_ref; change to warn+return\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_apply_plan_to_item` \u2014 same pattern; change to warn+return\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::update_item` \u2014 calls _rename_item_title and _apply_plan_to_item; no change needed (callers don't catch ValueError, so the uncaught raise propagates to them)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_auto_register_plan_artifact` \u2014 already uses safe skip pattern; reference implementation for the fix\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::close_item` \u2014 already uses safe skip pattern (fixed in #2656)\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 primary fix location; two functions require the safe-skip pattern\\n- `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` \u2014 source of the string nanoid issue_id_type; no change needed\\n- `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` \u2014 defines issue_id_type capability flag; no change needed\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 test gap: no tests cover the beads-nanoid path through _rename_item_title or _apply_plan_to_item; new tests needed\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [x] Every code consumer migrated to new interface (no migration needed \u2014 consumers benefit from no longer crashing)\\n- [x] Every stale document updated (none identified)\\n- [x] Every agent instruction updated (none identified)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n- [ ] Tests added for the new safe-skip path in both functions\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **_rename_item_title and _apply_plan_to_item raise valueerror for non-numeric issue refs if beads nanoids ever reach them** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code audit during close_item fix \u2014 operations.py (2026-06-20)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-21)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:25:44.324865Z</sub>\\n\\n**Reproducibility**: Latent \u2014 not directly triggerable in production today because the try_get_github() guard prevents entry into the vulnerable code path for beads backends. However, the bug is observable in unit tests by calling _rename_item_title or _apply_plan_to_item directly with a beads nanoid issue_ref and a non-None repository mock.\\n\\n**Reproduction steps (unit test)**:\\n1. Mock try_get_github to return a real Repository object\\n2. Call _rename_item_title(item, new_title=\\\"X\\\", issue_ref=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\", repo=mock_repo, out=out)\\n3. Observe: raises ValueError(\\\"Invalid issue ref: 'bd-a3f8'\\\") \u2014 not caught\\n\\n**After fix**: Same call logs a warning and returns True without raising.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:26:01.900435Z</sub>\\n\\n**Priority**: P2\\n**Effort**: S \u2014 Small. Two targeted one-line changes (replace raise ValueError with warn+return) at known locations in operations.py, plus two new unit tests. No design decisions required \u2014 the safe pattern is already established.\\n**Urgency**: Medium \u2014 latent bug; not crashing in production today but will crash if the try_get_github() guard is ever weakened or bypassed. Fixing it closes the design gap created when beads backend was introduced.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:26:37.000590Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `update_item` is called for a beads-backend item with a nanoid selector (e.g., `\\\"bd-a3f8\\\"`), helper functions that perform GitHub-specific operations (`_rename_item_title`, `_apply_plan_to_item`) should detect that the `issue_ref` is not a numeric GitHub issue number, log a warning that the operation is not applicable, and return without raising. The item update continues for the operations that are applicable to the beads backend.\\n\\nThis matches the behavior already present in `_auto_register_plan_artifact` and `close_item`.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:26:19.928015Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `_rename_item_title` called with a beads nanoid `issue_ref` emits a warning and returns without raising an exception\\n2. `_apply_plan_to_item` called with a beads nanoid `issue_ref` emits a warning and returns without raising an exception\\n3. Both functions continue to call `repository.get_issue(num).edit(title=...)` and the plan artifact path update for valid numeric `issue_ref` values (GitHub backend behavior is unchanged)\\n4. `test_rename_item_title_skips_for_beads_nanoid` passes: calling the function with `issue_ref=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\"` and a mocked non-None repository produces a warning in `out` and returns without raising\\n5. `test_apply_plan_to_item_skips_for_beads_nanoid` passes: same verification for `_apply_plan_to_item`\\n6. `uv run pytest tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` exits 0\\n7. `uv run prek run --files backlog_core/operations.py` exits 0\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:27:12.637708Z</sub>\\n\\n- Prior fix: commit 600e3e1e (issue #2656) \u2014 close_item safe-skip pattern; reference implementation\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_auto_register_plan_artifact` \u2014 second reference for the safe-skip pattern\\n- `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py::issue_id_type` \u2014 capability flag used to detect string-ID backends\\n</div>\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:26:55.810626Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 primary fix: _rename_item_title (~line 722) and _apply_plan_to_item (~line 770)\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 new tests for the beads-nanoid skip path in both functions\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:27:30.181133Z</sub>\\n\\n- No blocking dependencies. The fix is self-contained in operations.py.\\n- Related: #2664 (backlog_view routing gate for beads nanoids) \u2014 independent fix, can be implemented in the same PR.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:27:46.592625Z</sub>\\n\\n**Estimate**: S (Small) \u2014 2\u20134 hours\\n- 2 one-line code changes in operations.py (replace raise ValueError with warn+return)\\n- 2 new unit tests\\n- Linting pass\\n- No design decisions, no new dependencies, no schema changes\\n</div>\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:25:24.566931Z</sub>\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe fix aligns with the backlog server's design intent to support multiple backends (GitHub and Beads) transparently. The existing safe-skip pattern in _auto_register_plan_artifact and close_item establishes that GitHub-only operations should gracefully no-op for non-numeric selectors rather than crash. This fix extends that established pattern to two remaining functions, making backend handling consistent across all update-item helpers.\\n\\n**Supporting evidence**:\\n- Pattern already codified in close_item (commit 600e3e1e, issue #2656) \u2014 the design intent is documented by precedent\\n- _auto_register_plan_artifact uses identical safe-skip without ever having been flagged as a design concern\\n- No mission statement or architectural doc contradicts graceful skip behavior for non-applicable backends\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:24:01.741507Z</sub>\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:24:43.425933Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern\\n**Rationale**: The same design flaw \u2014 raising ValueError inside an except clause that does not catch ValueError \u2014 was previously identified and fixed in close_item (issue #2656, commit 600e3e1e). The pattern has now appeared again in _rename_item_title and _apply_plan_to_item. Two occurrences of the same root design error constitute a recurring pattern.\\n**Analysis Method**: 6-sigma frequency search \u2014 resolved backlog items show #2656 as prior fix for the identical pattern\\n**Scenario Target**: ValueError propagating uncaught from update_item operations for beads nanoid selectors \u2192 no crash today (try_get_github guard), but fragile design that will crash if the guard is ever removed or bypassed\\n</div>\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:25:05.829428Z</sub>\\n\\n**Pattern**: recurring-pattern \u2014 same root cause as #2656 (close_item)\\n\\n**Frequency measurement**: Grep(backlog_core/operations.py, pattern=\\\"raise ValueError\\\") found 2 active instances in _rename_item_title and _apply_plan_to_item after the #2656 fix removed the one in close_item. Prior to #2656 there were at least 3. Pattern has appeared in every function that calls parse_issue_number and was written before the beads backend was introduced.\\n\\n**Root cause**: When functions that call `parse_issue_number(issue_ref)` were written, the only backend was GitHub, so `issue_ref` was always a numeric string. The None-check was written as a defensive assertion (`raise ValueError`) rather than a graceful skip. When the beads backend was introduced, `issue_id_type = \\\"string\\\"` meant these functions could now receive nanoid selectors \u2014 but the `try_get_github()` null guard happened to prevent the code from being reached, masking the latent ValueError.\\n\\n**Design-level cause**: The ValueError raise is an incorrect response to a `None` result from `parse_issue_number`. The correct response for a GitHub-only operation receiving a non-numeric ID is to skip with a warning (the operation is not applicable to this backend). Raising treats a backend capability mismatch as a programmer error rather than a routing decision.\\n\\n**Improvement**: Apply the established safe-skip pattern uniformly to all functions that call parse_issue_number: when the result is None, log a warning and return \u2014 do not raise. Audit remaining raise ValueError usages in operations.py and replace them with the safe pattern.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bcab086fd19a4fde2c88211cddf46380295a9fa1dbf75ef9b87dbc37b8aed7b9\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCJd3Q\"}"}